   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## Step 1 \u2014 Resistance phenotype profile\n",
    "\n",
    "**Question this answers:** which resistance phenotypes exist, in which organisms, \n",
    "and which records should enter the resistance analysis?\n",
    "\n",
    "This step defines the outcome variable **Y** used by every later step.\n",
    "\n",
    "### The a priori applicability rule\n",
    "\n",
    "The six phenotypes are **bacterial** susceptibility categories. A *Candida* isolate \n",
    "with no CRE label does **not** mean \"Candida was sensitive\" \u2014 it means *the test \n",
    "does not exist for fungi*. Including ineligible organisms would inflate the denominator \n",
    "and understate resistance.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Eligibility is decided on microbiology, before looking at any outcome.**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Cell 1.1 \u2014 Flag each phenotype separately"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "PHENOTYPES = [\"CRE\", \"ESBL\", \"MDR\", \"VRE\", \"MRSA\", \"MRCONS\"]\n",
    "\n",
    "R = df[RES].astype(str).str.upper()\n",
    "\n",
    "for p in PHENOTYPES:\n",
    "    # \\b = word boundary: stops \"MRSA\" matching inside \"MRCONS\"\n",
    "    df[p] = R.str.contains(rf\"\\b{p}\\b\", regex=True, na=False).astype(int)\n",
    "\n",
    "# MSSA = methicillin-SENSITIVE: tracked separately, NEVER counted as resistant\n",
    "df[\"MSSA\"] = R.str.contains(r\"\\bMSSA\\b\", regex=True, na=False).astype(int)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Phenotype counts (raw, before applicability filter):\")\n",
    "print(df[PHENOTYPES + [\"MSSA\"]].sum().to_string())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Cell 1.2 \u2014 The a priori applicability rule (explicit organism sets)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Every one of the 136 organisms in the register is assigned to a class.\n",
    "# Using explicit sets (not a catch-all) makes the rule auditable.\n",
    "\n",
    "ENTEROBACTERALES = {\n",
    "    \"KLEBSIELLA PNEUMONIAE\",\"E. COLI\",\"PROTEUS MIRABILIS\",\"PROTEUS VULGARIS\",\n",
    "    \"PROTEUS SP\",\"SERRATIA MARCESCENS\",\"SERRATIA LIQUEFACIENS\",\"ENTEROBACTER SP\",\n",
    "    \"ENTEROBACTER CLOACAE\",\"CITROBACTER KOSERI\",\"CITROBACTER SP\",\"CITROBACTER FREUNDII\",\n",
    "    \"PROVIDENCIA SP\",\"PROVIDENCIA RETTGERI\",\"MORGANELLA MORGANII\"\n",
    "}\n",
    "NON_FERMENTERS = {\n",
    "    \"PSEUDOMONAS AERUGINOSA\",\"PSEUDOMONAS SP\",\"PSEUDOMONAS PUTIDA\",\"ACINETOBACTER SP\",\n",
    "    \"ACINETOBACTER LWOFFII\",\"ACINETOBACTER JUNII\",\"STENOTROPHOMONAS MALTOPHILIA\",\n",
    "    \"BURKHOLDERIA CEPACIA\",\"BURKHOLDERIA SP\",\"CHRYSEOBACTERIUM INDOLOGENES\",\n",
    "    \"CHRYSEOBACTERIUM SP\",\"ELIZABETHKINGIA MENINGOSEPTICA\",\"ACHROMOBACTER XYLOSOXIDANS\",\n",
    "    \"ACHROMOBACTER SP\",\"RALSTONIA PICKETTII\",\"RALSTONIA INSIDIOSA\",\"MYROIDES SP\",\n",
    "    \"SPHINGOMONAS PAUCIMOBILIS\",\"SPHINGOBACTERIUM SPIRITIVORUM\",\"SPHINGOBACTERIUM SP\",\n",
    "    \"COMAMONAS TESTOSTERONI\",\"OCHROBACTRUM ANTHROPI\"\n",
    "}\n",
    "ENTEROCOCCI = {\"ENTEROCOCCUS FAECIUM\",\"ENTEROCOCCUS FAECALIS\",\"ENTEROCOCCUS SP\"}\n",
    "S_AUREUS    = {\"STAPHYLOCOCCUS AUREUS\"}\n",
    "CONS        = {\n",
    "    \"STAPHYLOCOCCUS (COAGULASE NEGATIVE)\",\"STAPHYLOCOCCUS EPIDERMIDIS\",\n",
    "    \"STAPHYLOCOCCUS HAEMOLYTICUS\",\"STAPHYLOCOCCUS HOMINIS\",\n",
    "    \"STAPHYLOCOCCUS LUGDUNENSIS\",\"STAPHYLOCOCCUS SP\"\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "# Which phenotypes are DEFINED for each class \u2014 decided on microbiology, before seeing the data\n",
    "APPLICABLE = {\n",
    "    \"Enterobacterales\": [\"CRE\", \"ESBL\", \"MDR\"],   # CRE = carbapenem-resistant ENTEROBACTERALES\n",
    "    \"Non-fermenter\":    [\"MDR\"],                   # NOT CRE \u2014 Pseudomonas/Acinetobacter aren't Enterobacterales\n",
    "    \"Enterococcus\":     [\"VRE\"],\n",
    "    \"S. aureus\":        [\"MRSA\"],\n",
    "    \"CoNS\":             [\"MRCONS\"],\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "def classify_organism(o):\n",
    "    o = str(o).strip()\n",
    "    if o in ENTEROBACTERALES: return \"Enterobacterales\"\n",
    "    if o in NON_FERMENTERS:   return \"Non-fermenter\"\n",
    "    if o in ENTEROCOCCI:      return \"Enterococcus\"\n",
    "    if o in S_AUREUS:         return \"S. aureus\"\n",
    "    if o in CONS:             return \"CoNS\"\n",
    "    return \"INELIGIBLE\"     # fungi, viruses, mycobacteria, parasites, enteric pathogens, etc.\n",
    "\n",
    "df[\"org_class\"] = df[ORG].apply(classify_organism)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Organism class distribution:\")\n",
    "print(df[\"org_class\"].value_counts().to_string())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Cell 1.3 \u2014 Build the outcome Y"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "elig = df[df[\"org_class\"] != \"INELIGIBLE\"].copy()\n",
    "\n",
    "# A phenotype counts ONLY if it is both observed AND applicable to that organism\n",
    "for p in PHENOTYPES:\n",
    "    elig[\"valid_\" + p] = elig.apply(\n",
    "        lambda r, p=p: int(r[p] == 1 and p in APPLICABLE[r[\"org_class\"]]), axis=1)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Y = 1 if ANY applicable phenotype is present\n",
    "elig[\"Y\"] = elig[[\"valid_\" + p for p in PHENOTYPES]].max(axis=1)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Eligible isolates:  {len(elig):,}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Distinct samples:   {elig[SID].nunique():,}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Y = 1 (resistant):  {elig['Y'].sum():,}  ({100*elig['Y'].mean():.1f}%)\")\n",
    "print()\n",
    "print(\"Expected: 8,162 isolates \u00b7 7,336 samples \u00b7 4,491 resistant (55.0%)\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Cell 1.4 \u2014 Data-quality anomaly audit"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Runs on the WHOLE dataset \u2014 eligibility decides who enters the analysis;\n",
    "# the audit examines everyone, including ineligible organisms.\n",
    "\n",
    "anomalies = []\n",
    "for _, r in df.iterrows():\n",
    "    applicable = set(APPLICABLE.get(r[\"org_class\"], []))   # ineligible \u2192 empty set\n",
    "    for p in PHENOTYPES:\n",
    "        if r[p] == 1 and p not in applicable:\n",
    "            anomalies.append({\n",
    "                \"Sample ID\": r[SID],\n",
    "                \"Organism\":  r[ORG],\n",
    "                \"Class\":     r[\"org_class\"],\n",
    "                \"Phenotype\": p\n",
    "            })\n",
    "\n",
    "anom = pd.DataFrame(anomalies)\n",
    "print(f\"Anomalous organism\u2013phenotype records: {len(anom)}\")\n",
    "print()\n",
    "print(\"Breakdown:\")\n",
    "print(anom.groupby([\"Organism\", \"Phenotype\"]).size().rename(\"records\").to_string())\n",
    "print()\n",
    "print(\"These are documented and excluded from Y (not counted toward resistance).\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Cell 1.5 \u2014 Organism groups and resistance phenotype profile table"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def organism_group(r):\n",
    "    o = str(r[ORG]).upper()\n",
    "    c = r[\"org_class\"]\n",
    "    if \"KLEBSIELLA PNEUMONIAE\" in o: return \"Klebsiella pneumoniae\"\n",
    "    if o == \"E. COLI\":               return \"E. coli\"\n",
    "    if c == \"Enterobacterales\":      return \"Other Enterobacterales\"\n",
    "    if \"PSEUDOMONAS\" in o:           return \"Pseudomonas sp\"\n",
    "    if \"ACINETOBACTER\" in o:         return \"Acinetobacter sp\"\n",
    "    if c == \"Non-fermenter\":         return \"Other non-fermenters\"\n",
    "    if \"FAECIUM\" in o:               return \"Enterococcus faecium\"\n",
    "    if c == \"Enterococcus\":          return \"Other enterococci\"\n",
    "    if c == \"S. aureus\":             return \"Staphylococcus aureus\"\n",
    "    return \"Coagulase-negative staphylococci\"\n",
    "\n",
    "elig[\"organism_grp\"] = elig.apply(organism_group, axis=1)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Build the profile table\n",
    "# \"\u2014\" = not applicable  |  \"0.0%\" = applicable but not observed (two different meanings)\n",
    "rows = []\n",
    "for g, sub in elig.groupby(\"organism_grp\"):\n",
    "    app = APPLICABLE[sub[\"org_class\"].iloc[0]]      # every member of the group has the same class\n",
    "    row = {\"Organism group\": g, \"Isolates (n)\": len(sub)}\n",
    "    for p in PHENOTYPES:\n",
    "        row[p] = f\"{100*sub['valid_'+p].mean():.1f}%\" if p in app else \"\u2014\"\n",
    "    row[\"Any documented applicable resistance\"] = f\"{100*sub['Y'].mean():.1f}%\"\n",
    "    rows.append(row)\n",
    "\n",
    "profile = (pd.DataFrame(rows)\n",
    "             .sort_values(\"Isolates (n)\", ascending=False)\n",
    "             .reset_index(drop=True))\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"=== RESISTANCE PHENOTYPE PROFILE ===\")\n",
    "print(profile.to_string(index=False))\n",
    "print()\n",
    "print(\"Key: '\u2014' = phenotype not applicable  |  '0.0%' = applicable but zero observed\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## Step 2 \u2014 Bivariate associations (chi-square + Cram\u00e9r's V)\n",
    "\n",
    "**Question:** is each factor associated with resistance \u2014 and how strongly?\n",
    "\n",
    "**Important:** with 8,162 isolates, almost any difference will be statistically \n",
    "significant. Cram\u00e9r's V measures *how much* it matters, independently of sample size.\n",
    "\n",
    "| V | Strength |\n",
    "|---|---|\n",
    "| < 0.10 | Negligible |\n",
    "| 0.10\u20130.29 | Small |\n",
    "| 0.30\u20130.49 | Moderate |\n",
    "| \u2265 0.50 | Large |"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Cell 2.1 \u2014 Build the predictors"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# UNIT TYPE: critical care vs general ward\n",
    "CRIT_KEYWORDS = \"ICU|ITU|HDU|CCU|NICU|PICU|GITU|SICU|HDI\"\n",
    "elig[\"unit_grp\"] = np.where(\n",
    "    elig[UNIT].astype(str).str.upper().str.contains(CRIT_KEYWORDS),\n",
    "    \"Critical care\", \"General ward\"\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "# INFECTION ORIGIN\n",
    "elig[\"hai_grp\"] = np.where(\n",
    "    elig[HAI].astype(str).str.strip().str.upper() == \"HAI\",\n",
    "    \"HAI\", \"Community/outside\"\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "# SPECIMEN: keep the 6 most common individually, group the rest\n",
    "JUNK_SPEC = {\"OTHER / REVIEW\", \"(blank)\", \"OTHER / FLAGGED\", \"\"}\n",
    "ok = ~elig[SPEC].astype(str).str.strip().isin(JUNK_SPEC)\n",
    "top6 = elig.loc[ok, SPEC].value_counts().head(6).index\n",
    "elig[\"specimen_grp\"] = np.where(\n",
    "    elig[SPEC].isin(top6),\n",
    "    elig[SPEC].astype(str).str.title(),\n",
    "    \"Other\"\n",
    ")\n",
    "elig.loc[~ok, \"specimen_grp\"] = np.nan     # 15 unusable records excluded\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Predictor distributions:\")\n",
    "for c in [\"organism_grp\",\"specimen_grp\",\"unit_grp\",\"hai_grp\"]:\n",
    "    print(f\"\\n{c}  (n={elig[c].notna().sum():,})\")\n",
    "    print(elig[c].value_counts(dropna=False).head(6).to_string())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Cell 2.2 \u2014 Chi-square tests with effect sizes"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def cramers_v(ct, chi2):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Effect size for a contingency table: 0 = no association, 1 = perfect.\"\"\"\n",
    "    n = ct.values.sum()\n",
    "    return np.sqrt(chi2 / (n * (min(ct.shape) - 1)))\n",
    "\n",
    "def interpret_v(v):\n",
    "    if v >= 0.50: return \"Large\"\n",
    "    if v >= 0.30: return \"Moderate\"\n",
    "    if v >= 0.10: return \"Small\"\n",
    "    return \"Negligible\"\n",
    "\n",
    "results = []\n",
    "for label, col in [\n",
    "    (\"Organism group\",     \"organism_grp\"),\n",
    "    (\"Specimen type\",      \"specimen_grp\"),\n",
    "    (\"Hospital unit type\", \"unit_grp\"),\n",
    "    (\"HAI status\",         \"hai_grp\"),\n",
    "]:\n",
    "    d   = elig.dropna(subset=[col])\n",
    "    ct  = pd.crosstab(d[col], d[\"Y\"])\n",
    "    chi2, p, dof, expected = stats.chi2_contingency(ct)\n",
    "    v   = cramers_v(ct, chi2)\n",
    "\n",
    "    results.append({\n",
    "        \"Variable\":          label,\n",
    "        \"n\":                 ct.values.sum(),\n",
    "        \"\u03c7\u00b2\":               round(chi2, 2),\n",
    "        \"df\":                dof,\n",
    "        \"p\":                 p,\n",
    "        \"Cram\u00e9r's V\":        round(v, 3),\n",
    "        \"Strength\":          interpret_v(v),\n",
    "        \"Min expected count\": round(expected.min(), 1),\n",
    "    })\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Show the breakdown\n",
    "    pct = (ct[1] / ct.sum(axis=1) * 100).round(1)\n",
    "    tab = pd.DataFrame({\"n\": ct.sum(axis=1), \"resistant\": ct[1], \"% resistant\": pct})\n",
    "    print(f\"\\n=== {label} ===\")\n",
    "    print(tab.sort_values(\"% resistant\", ascending=False).to_string())\n",
    "    print(f\"  \u03c7\u00b2 = {chi2:.2f}  df = {dof}  p = {p:.2e}  V = {v:.3f}  ({interpret_v(v)})\")\n",
    "    print(f\"  min expected count = {expected.min():.1f}  (must be \u22655 for chi-square validity)\")\n",
    "\n",
    "summary2 = pd.DataFrame(results)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Holm\u2013Bonferroni correction for running four tests\n",
    "reject, p_adj, _, _ = multipletests(summary2[\"p\"], method=\"holm\")\n",
    "summary2[\"p (Holm)\"] = p_adj.round(6)\n",
    "summary2[\"Significant (\u03b1=0.05)\"] = np.where(reject, \"Yes\", \"No\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\n\\n=== SUMMARY TABLE ===\")\n",
    "print(summary2[[\"Variable\",\"n\",\"\u03c7\u00b2\",\"df\",\"p (Holm)\",\"Cram\u00e9r's V\",\"Strength\"]].to_string(index=False))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Cell 2.3 \u2014 Intraclass correlation and design effect"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# The data has one row per organism, so isolates from the same sample are correlated.\n",
    "# We quantify this rather than ignoring it.\n",
    "\n",
    "n = len(elig)\n",
    "k = elig[SID].nunique()\n",
    "mbar = n / k       # average isolates per sample\n",
    "\n",
    "grp  = elig.groupby(SID)[\"Y\"]\n",
    "ni   = grp.size().values\n",
    "yi   = grp.mean().values\n",
    "ybar = elig[\"Y\"].mean()\n",
    "\n",
    "MSB  = np.sum(ni * (yi - ybar) ** 2) / (k - 1)\n",
    "MSW  = np.sum([((s - s.mean()) ** 2).sum() for _, s in grp]) / (n - k)\n",
    "m0   = (n - np.sum(ni ** 2) / n) / (k - 1)\n",
    "\n",
    "icc  = (MSB - MSW) / (MSB + (m0 - 1) * MSW)\n",
    "deff = 1 + (mbar - 1) * icc\n",
    "eff_n = n / deff\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Average isolates per sample (m\u0304): {mbar:.4f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Intraclass correlation (ICC):    {icc:.4f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Design effect (DEFF):            {deff:.4f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Effective sample size:           {eff_n:.0f}  (vs raw n = {n:,})\")\n",
    "print()\n",
    "print(\"Note: DEFF \u2260 m\u0304.  DEFF = 1 + (m\u0304 \u2212 1) \u00d7 ICC\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Penalty is only ~{100*(deff-1):.1f}%, so conclusions are robust to clustering.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Cell 2.4 \u2014 Sensitivity analysis (one isolate per sample)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Re-run all four tests 200 times, each time keeping ONE random isolate per sample.\n",
    "# If the conclusions change, clustering matters. If they don't, they're robust.\n",
    "\n",
    "TESTS = [\n",
    "    (\"Organism group\",     \"organism_grp\"),\n",
    "    (\"Specimen type\",      \"specimen_grp\"),\n",
    "    (\"Hospital unit type\", \"unit_grp\"),\n",
    "    (\"HAI status\",         \"hai_grp\"),\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "sens_results = {lab: [] for lab, _ in TESTS}\n",
    "np.random.seed(42)\n",
    "\n",
    "for seed in range(200):\n",
    "    one = elig.sample(frac=1, random_state=seed).drop_duplicates(SID)\n",
    "    for lab, col in TESTS:\n",
    "        d  = one.dropna(subset=[col])\n",
    "        ct = pd.crosstab(d[col], d[\"Y\"])\n",
    "        chi2, p, _, _ = stats.chi2_contingency(ct)\n",
    "        sens_results[lab].append((cramers_v(ct, chi2), p))\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Sensitivity analysis \u2014 200 random one-isolate-per-sample replicates\\n\")\n",
    "print(f\"{'Variable':<22} {'Full V':>8} {'Mean V (sens)':>14} {'Sig in 200':>12}\")\n",
    "print(\"-\" * 60)\n",
    "\n",
    "for lab, col in TESTS:\n",
    "    full_ct  = pd.crosstab(elig.dropna(subset=[col])[col], elig.dropna(subset=[col])[\"Y\"])\n",
    "    full_v   = cramers_v(full_ct, stats.chi2_contingency(full_ct)[0])\n",
    "    mean_v   = np.mean([v for v, _ in sens_results[lab]])\n",
    "    n_sig    = sum(p < 0.05 for _, p in sens_results[lab])\n",
    "    print(f\"{lab:<22} {full_v:>8.3f} {mean_v:>14.3f} {n_sig:>10}/200\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print()\n",
    "print(\"Conclusion: effect sizes are stable and significance holds in every replicate.\")\n",
    "print(\"The bivariate results are robust to within-sample clustering.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## Step 3 \u2014 Logistic regression (inference + prediction)\n",
    "\n",
    "**Two questions in one model:**\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **Inference** \u2014 *which factors are independently associated with resistance,\n",
    "   after accounting for the others?* \u2192 adjusted odds ratios\n",
    "2. **Prediction** \u2014 *how well can the model estimate resistance for new isolates?* \n",
    "   \u2192 AUC, Brier score, calibration\n",
    "\n",
    "**Why logistic and not linear regression:**  \n",
    "The outcome is binary (resistant / not). Linear regression could predict \n",
    "values below 0 or above 1, which are meaningless. Logistic regression \n",
    "keeps fitted probabilities inside [0, 1] by modelling the log-odds.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Why cluster-robust standard errors:**  \n",
    "Two isolates from the same sample are correlated (ICC = 0.18). \n",
    "`cov_type=\"cluster\"` widens the SEs appropriately.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Why grouped splitting:**  \n",
    "If we split by *row*, two organisms from the same sample could land on \n",
    "different sides \u2014 the model sees part of a specimen while training and \n",
    "is tested on the rest. That inflates AUC. Splitting by *Sample ID* \n",
    "keeps every specimen wholly on one side."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Cell 3.1 \u2014 Pre-model diagnostics"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "d = elig.dropna(subset=[\"specimen_grp\"]).rename(columns={SID: \"sample_id\"}).copy()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Modelling population: {len(d):,} isolates from {d['sample_id'].nunique():,} samples\")\n",
    "print()\n",
    "\n",
    "# (a) SEPARATION: no category may be 0% or 100% resistant\n",
    "print(\"(a) Separation check:\")\n",
    "for col in [\"organism_grp\",\"specimen_grp\",\"unit_grp\",\"hai_grp\"]:\n",
    "    t = d.groupby(col)[\"Y\"].agg(n=\"size\", events=\"sum\")\n",
    "    t[\"pct\"] = (100 * t.events / t.n).round(1)\n",
    "    bad = t[(t.events == 0) | (t.events == t.n)]\n",
    "    status = \"PASS \u2014 no separation\" if len(bad) == 0 else f\"FAIL \u2014 {list(bad.index)}\"\n",
    "    print(f\"  {col:22s}: {status}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# (b) EVENTS PER PARAMETER\n",
    "n_params = ((d.organism_grp.nunique()-1) + (d.specimen_grp.nunique()-1) + 1 + 1)\n",
    "epv = d[\"Y\"].sum() / n_params\n",
    "print(f\"\\n(b) Events per parameter: {d['Y'].sum():,} events / {n_params} parameters = {epv:.0f}  (rule of thumb \u226510)\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# (c) MULTICOLLINEARITY (VIF)\n",
    "X = pd.get_dummies(d[[\"organism_grp\",\"specimen_grp\",\"unit_grp\",\"hai_grp\"]], drop_first=True).astype(float)\n",
    "X = sm.add_constant(X)\n",
    "vif = pd.DataFrame({\n",
    "    \"variable\": X.columns,\n",
    "    \"VIF\": [variance_inflation_factor(X.values, i) for i in range(X.shape[1])]\n",
    "})\n",
    "vif = vif[vif.variable != \"const\"].sort_values(\"VIF\", ascending=False)\n",
    "print(f\"\\n(c) Max VIF: {vif.VIF.max():.2f}  (rule of thumb <5)\")\n",
    "print()\n",
    "print(\"All three checks pass.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Cell 3.2 \u2014 Fit the model (cluster-robust standard errors)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Reference categories chosen for interpretability:\n",
    "#   Organism   \u2192 E. coli  (most common Enterobacterales)\n",
    "#   Specimen   \u2192 Urine    (most common)\n",
    "#   Unit       \u2192 General ward\n",
    "#   Origin     \u2192 Community/outside\n",
    "\n",
    "formula = (\n",
    "    \"Y ~ C(organism_grp, Treatment(reference='E. coli'))\"\n",
    "    \" + C(specimen_grp,  Treatment(reference='Urine'))\"\n",
    "    \" + C(unit_grp,      Treatment(reference='General ward'))\"\n",
    "    \" + C(hai_grp,       Treatment(reference='Community/outside'))\"\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "model_naive   = smf.logit(formula, data=d).fit(disp=0)        # for pseudo-R\u00b2\n",
    "model_cluster = smf.logit(formula, data=d).fit(\n",
    "    disp=0,\n",
    "    cov_type=\"cluster\",\n",
    "    cov_kwds={\"groups\": d[\"sample_id\"]},\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"n = {int(model_cluster.nobs):,}  |  pseudo-R\u00b2 = {model_naive.prsquared:.4f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Likelihood-ratio test  p = {model_naive.llr_pvalue:.2e}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Cell 3.3 \u2014 Extract and display odds ratios"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "ci = model_cluster.conf_int()\n",
    "\n",
    "OR = pd.DataFrame({\n",
    "    \"OR\":      np.exp(model_cluster.params),\n",
    "    \"CI_low\":  np.exp(ci[0]),\n",
    "    \"CI_high\": np.exp(ci[1]),\n",
    "    \"p\":       model_cluster.pvalues,\n",
    "}).drop(\"Intercept\").round(3)\n",
    "\n",
    "OR[\"significant\"] = np.where(OR.p < 0.05, \"***\", \"\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Adjusted odds ratios (cluster-robust 95% CIs)\")\n",
    "print(\"Reference: E. coli / Urine / General ward / Community origin\")\n",
    "print()\n",
    "print(OR.to_string())\n",
    "print()\n",
    "print(\"OR > 1 \u2192 higher odds of resistance vs reference\")\n",
    "print(\"OR < 1 \u2192 lower  odds of resistance vs reference\")\n",
    "print(\"CI excludes 1 \u2192 statistically significant\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Cell 3.4 \u2014 Prediction: grouped train / test split"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# GroupShuffleSplit keeps every sample on ONE side of the split.\n",
    "# This prevents leakage when a sample has multiple isolates.\n",
    "\n",
    "splitter = GroupShuffleSplit(n_splits=1, test_size=0.25, random_state=42)\n",
    "train_i, test_i = next(splitter.split(d, d[\"Y\"], groups=d[\"sample_id\"]))\n",
    "train, test = d.iloc[train_i].copy(), d.iloc[test_i].copy()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Train: {len(train):,} isolates from {train.sample_id.nunique():,} samples\")\n",
    "print(f\"Test:  {len(test):,} isolates from {test.sample_id.nunique():,} samples\")\n",
    "print(f\"Sample overlap: {len(set(train.sample_id) & set(test.sample_id))}  (must be 0)\")\n",
    "print(f\"Resistant rate \u2014 train: {100*train.Y.mean():.1f}%  |  test: {100*test.Y.mean():.1f}%\")\n",
    "\n",
    "model_train = smf.logit(formula, data=train).fit(disp=0)\n",
    "test = test.copy()\n",
    "test[\"p_resist\"] = model_train.predict(test)\n",
    "\n",
    "auc   = roc_auc_score(test[\"Y\"], test[\"p_resist\"])\n",
    "brier = brier_score_loss(test[\"Y\"], test[\"p_resist\"])\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"\\nAUC   = {auc:.4f}  (0.5 = chance, 1.0 = perfect)\")\n",
    "print(f\"Brier = {brier:.4f}  (0.25 = uninformative at this prevalence)\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Cell 3.5 \u2014 Threshold performance table"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "rows = []\n",
    "for th in [0.30, 0.40, 0.50, 0.60, 0.70]:\n",
    "    pred = (test[\"p_resist\"] >= th).astype(int)\n",
    "    tn, fp, fn, tp = confusion_matrix(test[\"Y\"], pred).ravel()\n",
    "    rows.append({\n",
    "        \"Threshold\":   th,\n",
    "        \"Sensitivity\": round(tp / (tp + fn), 3),\n",
    "        \"Specificity\": round(tn / (tn + fp), 3),\n",
    "        \"PPV\":         round(tp / (tp + fp), 3),\n",
    "        \"Accuracy\":    round((tp + tn) / len(test), 3),\n",
    "    })\n",
    "\n",
    "th_table = pd.DataFrame(rows)\n",
    "print(th_table.to_string(index=False))\n",
    "print()\n",
    "print(\"Note: 0.5 is a conventional threshold, not clinically optimised.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Cell 3.6 \u2014 Calibration"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "test[\"decile\"] = pd.qcut(test[\"p_resist\"], 10, labels=False, duplicates=\"drop\")\n",
    "\n",
    "calib = (test.groupby(\"decile\")\n",
    "             .agg(n=(\"Y\",\"size\"), predicted=(\"p_resist\",\"mean\"), observed=(\"Y\",\"mean\"))\n",
    "             .round(3))\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Calibration by decile of predicted risk:\")\n",
    "print(calib.to_string())\n",
    "print()\n",
    "print(\"Well-calibrated = predicted \u2248 observed in every row.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Cell 3.7 \u2014 Grouped 5-fold cross-validation"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Folds are grouped by Sample ID \u2014 same leakage-prevention logic as the train/test split.\n",
    "\n",
    "cv_aucs   = []\n",
    "cv_briers = []\n",
    "\n",
    "for tr_i, te_i in GroupKFold(n_splits=5).split(d, d[\"Y\"], groups=d[\"sample_id\"]):\n",
    "    m  = smf.logit(formula, data=d.iloc[tr_i]).fit(disp=0)\n",
    "    pp = m.predict(d.iloc[te_i])\n",
    "    cv_aucs.append(roc_auc_score(d.iloc[te_i][\"Y\"], pp))\n",
    "    cv_briers.append(brier_score_loss(d.iloc[te_i][\"Y\"], pp))\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"5-fold grouped cross-validation:\")\n",
    "print(f\"  AUC per fold:  {np.round(cv_aucs, 4).tolist()}\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Mean AUC:      {np.mean(cv_aucs):.4f}  (SD {np.std(cv_aucs):.4f})\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Mean Brier:    {np.mean(cv_briers):.4f}\")\n",
    "print()\n",
    "print(\"Small SD \u2192 performance is stable, not an artefact of one lucky split.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## Step 4 \u2014 Statistical process control (p-chart)\n",
    "\n",
    "**Question:** is the HAI rate really changing, or is this just normal month-to-month noise?\n",
    "\n",
    "A p-chart plots the monthly proportion with **control limits** that mark the \n",
    "boundary of normal variation. A point outside the limits, or a run of 8+ months \n",
    "on one side of the centre line, is a genuine signal \u2014 not noise.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Why variable control limits?**  \n",
    "The standard error is \u221a(p\u0304(1\u2212p\u0304)/n\u209c), which depends on that month's sample count.  \n",
    "Since denominators range from 721 to 854, drawing a single flat pair of lines \n",
    "would be wrong. Limits are computed separately for each month.\n",
    "\n",
    "**What this monitors:**  \n",
    "The monthly proportion of culture-positive *samples* classified as HAI.  \n",
    "This is NOT a true incidence rate \u2014 patient-day denominators were not available."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Cell 4.1 \u2014 Aggregate to sample level by month"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],